From: Lars Karlslund <lars@karlslund.dk>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: t14s: disable crypto for interconnect sync_state

Sleep test build only. The interconnect providers keep the firmware's
boot-time votes until sync_state, which waits for every DT consumer to bind.
QCE has no driver (CRYPTO_DEV_QCE is not built), so the votes are never
dropped and DDR/buses stay at boot level through suspend.
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e78100-lenovo-thinkpad-t14s.dtsi	2026-10-20 19:09:22.784021462 +0200
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e78100-lenovo-thinkpad-t14s.dtsi	2026-10-20 19:09:22.794153800 +0200
@@ -2264,3 +2264,12 @@
 
 	};
 };
+
+/*
+ * Sleep test build: let the interconnect providers reach sync_state and drop
+ * the firmware's boot-time votes. They otherwise wait forever for QCE, which
+ * has no driver here (CRYPTO_DEV_QCE is not built).
+ */
+&crypto {
+	status = "disabled";
+};
